Abstract

This document specifies a 2026–2055 research program for trustworthy, verifiable, energy-aware intelligence under explicit physical, epistemic, and governance constraints. It replaces calendar dependency with a readiness-level partial order, sequential PhD phases with parallel tracks under a cross-track non-blocking rule, verification promises with assurance cases and interface-level proofs, and a scalar objective with a non-scalarised proxy vector and an explicit two-stage Pareto-then-decision protocol. It scopes one falsifiable dissertation (GCRP 2, Verified Multi-Agent Intelligence) as the empirical gate for all downstream programs. All programs are at RL0. The document's credibility derives from its killability: every claim is stated so that a future experiment can falsify it.

