2. Guiding Principle

Principle. Build trustworthy, verifiable, energy-aware intelligence before delegating civilisation-scale autonomy — while keeping humans accountable, institutions polycentric, and physical limits explicit.

Corollary 2.1 (Verification–assurance partition). Where formal verification is feasible, use it. Where it is not, use audited assurance cases with explicit residual-risk registers. Graceful degradation is mandatory and must be certified, not asserted.

Corollary 2.2 (Volume–rigor separation). Volume is not rigor. A twelve-program roadmap without one defended dissertation scope is decorative.

Corollary 2.3 (Compression operator). \text{Portfolio} \rightarrow \text{research context} \rightarrow \text{one falsifiable problem} \rightarrow \text{one experimental system} \rightarrow \text{one contribution}.

